bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:1:<<!DOCTYPE "memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki" "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext">>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:10:role      = "the W29 lane's kit: the place KEL arms (an inception commits a next cold key, a rotation reveals it from the founding card), the five floor duties sign one framed image, peers learn the head through the carriage board and the carry bundle, and a seed census names every raw-seed consumer"
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:13:type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:23:The floor trust chain orders its pin claims by place-KEL descent, so the place KEL carries a sequence, a digest chain and a committed next key. X0 bakes the pre-rotation and the scoped signer; each member of X0 carries its own readiness red, and this lane builds them (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> :207, :544).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:34:* ''The card ceremony.'' The cold key rests on a founding card alone: its seed reaches no file. A founding and every rotation read the card back through an injected `PlaceFoundingCard` before a byte lands (the CLI adapts `cold-card-readback`; a staged test root stands in). A rotation runs under one custody claim: verify the card against the head, mint the next cold key and the replacement signer, read the replacement card back, stage the signed event with the replacement signer durably (`.vessel-rotating*.json`), publish the chain and the key file, remove the stage. A restart reconciles a staged file against the last verified head and never invents a successor; a staged file with no read-back card, or of another head, refuses.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:36:* ''The framed duties.'' The five floor duties (carriage carrier, place floor pin, flow pointer, raise challenge, gate place finish) sign and verify one image `u32 len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` (`frameFloorDuty`, `floorDutyOf`, `verifyPlaceDuty`, `verifyPlaceDutyAtHead` in `place-signer.ts`). The KEL events sign under the KEL grammar, never a sixth floor domain.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:37:* ''The seed census.'' `tools/seed-census.mjs` names every raw-seed consumer against an explicit list, proves itself on a planted consumer, and fails on any new consumer or stale entry. The K15 entries ride it as named owed exceptions in `{rule, file, match, count, reason}` shape, and K15 burns each when its bond lands.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:49:# ''Built ~ the seed census'' (`tools/seed-census{.mjs,.test.mjs,-witness.sh}`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:50:# ''Built ~ the browser founding'' (`browser-vessel-identity.ts`: `foundBrowserPlaceKel`, `loadBrowserPlaceKel`, `readBrowserPlaceHead`). A leaf mints the armed inception through the same mesh grammar and reads its cold card back through the same `PlaceFoundingCard` port (`place-founding-card.ts` in mesh). A leaf holds no floor, so with no ceremony seated the identity open founds the device key and no KEL, and the explicit door refuses `PlaceFoundingCardUnread` until a ceremony UI seats a card (`placeFoundingCard` on `openBrowserVessel`). Heads read through the one `foldPlaceKel`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:54:# ''Owed ~ the readers by head.'' The four duty verifiers verify under the key a caller passes; the floor pin claim lane (W14 to W16) resolves each duty's signer through `verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`. Names that key a place by its inception key follow the head when that lane lands.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:56:# ''Owed ~ K15's bonds.'' The vessel-wide Keyhive Individual and place card, the bare place leaf, the relay key, daemon auth, device and face work, internal asks and `lares meme` signing stay on the seed census as named K15 exceptions.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:67:# The seed census reads its list exactly, and a planted consumer turns it red.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:1:<<!DOCTYPE "memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki" "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext">>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:10:role      = "the Wave C lane's kit: K15 step 6, the fence, under the identity model the operator approved on 2026-10-20 (sync carries; verification decides): the sealed identity anchor, the signed @persona log, verified projections, each face's D rows sealed under its own key, the daemon's last singletons split by face, and the browser's per-face planes"
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:13:type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:23:Wave C builds `K15` step 6, the fence, under one identity model the operator approved on 2026-10-20: //sync carries; verification decides// (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> #/rulings; the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">>). Beneath it stands the moʻolelo's first line: the truth rests in the minds of the operators, and the CRDTs carry it to the synced stores. Wave C launches once Wave B lands on a green span; `W26`'s slices 3, 4 and 6 run beside it on the floor's own ground; its slice 5 follows, since the accepted floor rests as a face's D row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:31:''Kalani's laptop forgets nothing it swore to.'' Someone with write access to Kalani's synced docs rewrites the daemon doc to name another face's group and KEL prefix, with a perfectly valid edge from that other face. Kalani's laptop boots, reads its own sealed anchor, sees a bundle it never swore to, and refuses by name. The crier shouted a lie; the stone kept the name.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:33:''The Council's lease never runs backward.'' A stale replica of the Council's daemon doc arrives missing the newest lease slot. Before Wave C, an old device edge reads current against it. After it, each device keeps a sealed frontier that never falls, and the stale replica moves nothing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:47:# ''The sealed anchor.'' Each face holds, on each device, a D row: its PersonaGroup, persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Founding, admission and the recovery rites write it; sync never does. Red: a forged selector row in the daemon doc, then a coherent valid foreign bundle, switch no pinned face; a missing anchor refuses face boot by name.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:50:# ''Verified projections.'' The face planes and the daemon doc's identity tiddlers read as projections of verified records, disposable and rebuilt. Red: a plane URL with no signed founding or admission act behind it never registers.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:51:# ''The FCK fence.'' Each face's D rows (atom, archive, anchor, custody root, proof keys) seal under that face's own random FCK and key by its PersonaGroup on both hosts; the vessel key opens none of them. Red: K15's isolation red at the key-class level, where Wave B's `test.fails` rows turn green: unlock A alone, and every key A holds, the vessel key included, opens no B row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:52:# ''The daemon's last unions'' (Wave B's census, node items 4 to 6): one keyhive, face ledger, content-key seat and seat-roll set per face, never one per daemon; face-join and seat duties reseal the asking face's bags alone; CLI selectors name their face and never default to `h0`; `fleet-join-pending` keys by face; a joined face's hearth dial pin stands per face.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:54:# ''The house holder answers, never stalls'' (Wave B's seventh fresh read, carried). A floor or house worker that never announces `ready` refuses its held asks by name and is never left waiting; a replay posts its replacement manifest before it retires the crossing it replaces; a missing seat-roll ledger keeps one pending find per document, never one per gate read; the C4 boot trace's manifest marker fires on the real source, proven by a control that runs `instrumentBootSource` over the daemon and counts one `host:manifest-post`; the pre-clear `doc:rested` carries a storage proof from the house's own rest shore. Red: each of these, every one through an event or causal read, never a timer that decides.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:72:One joint lane (`feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--k15-wave-c`), one pull request, landed whole and merged by train. A Sonnet Episkopos leads; the Codex Sol (`gpt-6-sol`, walled) builds; the Copilot seat (`gpt-5.3-codex`) reads, scouts and sweeps (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">>). The battery rides CI's shards: locally the wave runs its build and each red's proof against the base tree, pushes once, and reads lane CI, held-out and the shards. A fresh Sol reader, from a lineage that built none of it, reads the whole diff before the train. The scout census opens the lane: every place an identity pin reads from a mutable doc without verification, by file and line, sorted by what inherits shape from what.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:76:<<~ ahu #/owed>>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:80:* ''The recovery door: guardian-quorum rotation, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the log and frontier.'' No production door rotates a persona root beneath its KEL prefix: `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function with its red and control (a face recovered to a new root boots against the rewritten anchor; a document naming the new root with no KEL rotation behind it refuses), and `runReadmitEdge` has no production caller. Building the door means the guardian-quorum ceremony, whose guardian count is an open operator gate (`kahu#/seed-and-nexus`). The re-admit then carries the current `@persona` log and the signed frontier as a first admit does.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:82:* ''A face's circles and identities follow the face'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-22): minted once at founding, named by a signed `plane` act, carried in the admit bundle, adopted by every admitted device, and named in the face proof beside the persona plane (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-circle">> #/the-atom). Sessions stay per vessel, as motion.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:85:* ''A browser holding several faces'' takes the dedicated-worker floor (`houseOfBoot` reads the founding bootstrap and refuses when more than one persona root stands), and its worn second face proves its persona plane alone: the founding bootstrap names one face's circles and identities. Both ride Wave D's browser mirror (slice 4), where each face keeps its own documents and key.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:86:* ''A joinee that boots from its daemon-carried act bundle'' keeps that projection until a reboot when a later persona-plane replica carries a competing same-sequence act. The arrival-triggered re-proof and what it does on a fork belong to K18, beside the recovery door and the equivocation handling.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:87:* ''End-to-end gate controls'': the faced-boot composer controls read source order and the admit door's face-edge suite mocks the log projection and the lease read; a sealed-vessel run that inspects catalog side effects, and the real-engine holder lifecycle in a browser whose module graph greets (the Chromium and Firefox harness here floors, so those cases skip), ride the container weld in `tools/mesh-scenarios.sh`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:89:* ''The holder door takes the user's cancel'': `attachSharedHolder` sets no deadline, so a worker that neither greets nor errors waits forever. Every production caller passes a `signal` tied to the user's intent (the tab closing, a face switch, a user abort). `open-browser-vessel.ts` holds no such signal today (`BrowserVesselOptions` carries none), so the wiring and its red (a silent worker plus a user abort floors the boot at once) ride the first lane that gives the vessel open an abort path.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:90:* ''K15-H: the Handle owner rides the anchor'' (a new lane, scheduled after Wave C beside Wave D where the file sets prove disjoint; K18 owns the recovery door, not this). Scope: Handle founding, burn and rotation take the owner prefix from the sealed anchor through `readFace`, and `headOpKey` goes behind the door on both shores. The census (`face-reading-census.test.ts`) names the files by spelling until they migrate: `commands/handle.ts`, `browser-handle-verbs.ts` and `handle-publish.ts`. Read 4's two findings, verbatim. FINDING 1: MEASURED — `packages/lararium-mesh/src/handle-publish.ts:25-46`; `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/handle.ts:47-79`; `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-handle-publish.ts:23-40` — Handle founding takes its owner Persona KEL prefix straight from a mutable daemon tiddler, outside `readFace`. The seed is loaded by selected handle index, but `publishHandleFromDaemonDoc` never checks the selected face's sealed anchor, signed founding act, or verified KEL lineage. A daemon-document change can choose a foreign or stale prefix for the signed public Handle inception. The downstream Handle chain treats the owner prefix as part of its own signed inception, so the local signer can permanently publish the wrong owner binding even when the face boot would reject that selector. The census contains none of `publishHandleFromDaemonDoc`, `PERSONA_KEL_PREFIX_TIDDLER`, or `publishPersonaGlamour` in its primitive or decision-site lists. FINDING 2: MEASURED — `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/handle.ts:224-235,269-281`; `packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-handle-verbs.ts:123-141` — owner burn and Handle rotation resolve owner authority from the mutable daemon prefix through a separate `headOpKey` verifier, outside `readFace`. These commands take `PERSONA_KEL_PREFIX_TIDDLER` from the daemon doc, resolve its board chain, and accept a matching root seed as the authorizing hand. The check proves that *some* chain has that current key; it does not prove that this Handle's owner member prefix is the selected face's sealed anchor prefix or the Handle inception's owner set. The Handle KEL's own membership verifier may still reject a mismatched owner prefix; the direct authority decision at the local command is nonetheless outside the door, and the census misses the entire `headOpKey` spelling. The same raw-prefix pattern serves both Node and browser.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:93:* ''Read 6's two lane-owned HIGH, written verbatim as Wave D's opening rows'' (read 6 found no P0: an unaffiliated wire peer reached no face act and no private plane). ROW 1: MEASURED — lane-owned composition, foreign face share falls open when its catalog row is absent. `packages/lararium-node/src/face-fleet-view.ts:76-87,131-137`; `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:753-754`. One-line reason: the worn face bridge allows *every* document id outside a negative set derived from the mutable catalog, so deleting or withholding a foreign face's row before a new session is seated removes that face's private plane from the deny set. This is the exact inverse of the proposed authority direction: an unverified catalog *absence* changes a share from false to true. The `bb8513247` repair added `foreignFaceDocs`, but the live verdict is `view.fetch(id).ok || !others.has(id)`; a missing catalog entry makes `others.has` false. The source test itself demonstrates the relevant behavior at `face-fleet-view.test.ts:122-140`: with only the worn bootstrap, the bare bridge reads the other face's circles, and supplying a catalog-derived `foreign` set blocks it. The control never tries the catalog row deleted after registration, or a held other-face document whose catalog entry was omitted. A same-operator session of the worn face can fetch the other face's held document by id in that state. The verdict is wired through `shareConfigOf` to both the announce and access hooks (`federation-gate.ts:602-611`), so this is an access decision rather than an announcement-only cosmetic leak; the live transport control at `share-policy-is-access.test.ts:49-67` demonstrates that distinction. This is not P0 under the user's definition because the reader already has an admitted face; the leak crosses face compartments on one vessel. The authorization decision must come from the sealed/proven face-document inventory or a positive view, rather than catalog completeness. The broad bridge predates Wave C (Wave B/O1), but Wave C owns the `foreignFaceDocs` repair and its composer wiring; this finding concerns that lane-owned repair, not the inherited bridge in isolation. ROW 2: MEASURED — lane-owned node daemon keeps a lease floor older than the sealed anchor it raises at boot. `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:2260-2271,2311-2346`; `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts:306-321,421-423,704-743,986-1008`; `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/lease-frontier.ts:64-70`. One-line reason: the composer snapshots `standingAnchor` into `daemonAuth` and awaits `openDaemonVm` *before* it raises and persists the verified lease epoch; the running daemon's live join and grant reads keep flooring under the old object. For a concrete counterexample, start with sealed lease epoch 0 and a verified signed advance to 7 in the mirrored daemon doc. The daemon receives anchor 0, starts, then the parent persists anchor 7 at `:2346`. If that mutable slot is deleted or replayed to 0 during the same daemon lifetime, `readLeaseUnderFace` reads 0 and floors against the daemon's captured anchor 0, despite custody now pinning 7. Its live face-join at `operator-daemon-behavior.ts:704-743` passes the lowered `lease.n` into a new seat and re-seal, while grant ingest at `:306-321` verifies an older bound. A restart loads 7 and closes the window; the claim that the sealed frontier never falls in a standing daemon does not hold. This is Wave C's lease-observation and composer ordering, not an inherited timer. The seam should raise the anchor before forming/sending `daemonAuth`, or deliver the raised pin to the daemon through a verified update. The existing red at `signed-lease-frontier.test.ts:50-61` hands `readLeaseUnderFace` an anchor already at 7, and `lease-observation.test.ts:26` tests the pure raise, so both can pass while the composer sends 0 before it persists 7. A red needs the live daemon, a signed advance, a subsequent slot deletion, and a control that the older edge or grant remains refused without restart.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:103:* ''The far agent's relay seat'': its research after `I1`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:104:* ''The signer frames each floor duty's domain'': `X0`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:1:<<!DOCTYPE "memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki" "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext">>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:9:role      = "kit: K15 step 0, the custody contract before bytes move — the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the face custody key, the carrier binding, the overwrite contract, the one-face bundle, the reds per vessel, the build order and the open joints; drafted by a Sol-6 spirit over four research rounds, verified against code"
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:14:type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:32:Every persisted custody carrier and every act that touches it has exactly one target class. ''D'' dissolves confidential material into rows owned by one PersonaGroup and sealed with that group's face custody key (FCK). ''F'' carries deliberately public material or ciphertext a blind floor may copy; it has no custody decryption key. ''S'' carries a *named* node-only confidential row under a named node principal and opener. A shared verb creates no shared key. A mixed carrier splits before it receives a class. The browser has no vessel custody key (S key). A node has no residual omnibus key: only an actual S row can justify a node custody door. Current `hot`/`cold` mean S-sealed, not target ownership (`vault-carriers.ts:5-22,64-68`). These are operator rulings recorded at `stable-founding-road.mem:205-207`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:38:<<~ ahu #/row-census-node>>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:40:!!! Row census — node
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:46:| `vessel-key` `:240-242` | floor | ''S, OPEN JOINT:'' private place signing seed owned by this node. Its public verifying key belongs in F. The signer options appear below; it is never a custody S key or face ancestor. `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442,451-487` proves the private seed is read from disk and used at the floor door. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:47:| `vessel-kel` `:243-245` | floor | ''F:'' public armed chain (inception and rotations), node place principal. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:48:| `vessel-rotating` | floor | ''S:'' the staged replacement signer and its signed rotation, present only between a rotation's stage and publish. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:49:| `s-slots` `:246-248` | floor | ''D/S split:'' the node S tree wraps one random S key and seals `gate-root` and `place-archive` alone. Each face has its own FCK tree, and no face FCK wraps under a node key. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:50:| `sk-slots` `:249-251` | floor | ''S conditional, node:'' retire current S-key-to-SK wrapping. No serving row exists today (`:12-14`). A future serving payload gets its own named S key and boot rule before this tree survives. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:51:| `fk-slots` `face-custody.ts` | floor | ''D (the face's own tree):'' one tree per face at `faces/<fcid>/fk-slots.bin`, wrapping that face's random custody key under each human route that face asked for. No S key wraps it and no sibling face's route opens it; the face's rows and this tree rest in one directory, so a bundle or a removal moves them together. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:52:| `face-index` `face-index.ts` | floor-plain | ''F:'' the one floor row that names the faces a node can unlock before any face opens: the count of faces (tombstones included), each group's digest, each founding ask's digest and each random directory name, and no other byte. It routes and never decides; see #/the-floor-index. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:53:| `vessel-card` `:254-256` | floor-plain | ''F:'' public node contact card. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:54:| `charter` `:257-259` | floor-plain | ''F:'' signed public founding charter. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:55:| `carried-charter` `:260-262` | floor-plain | ''F:'' signed public carried charter. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:56:| `carriage-consent` `:263-265` | floor-plain | ''F:'' public consent/pin as the row comment defines it. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:57:| `nexus-key-line` `:266-268` | floor-plain | ''F:'' public hand-over keys/signatures. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:58:| `carriage-admit` `:269-271` | floor-plain | ''F:'' public gate reach/pin. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:59:| `sealed-rest` `:275-277` | floor-plain | ''F carriage:'' sealed lockboxes, signed records and indexes remain opaque transport; cryptographic content ownership stays with the relevant face's Keyhive/content-key seat. The row is not an FCK escrow. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:60:| `sealed-own` `:279-281` | floor-plain | ''F only for proved opaque pointers/marks. LEAD:'' audit names and values for face-linking metadata; any private index dissolves into D. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:61:| `sealed-chunk` `:283-285` | floor-plain | ''F carriage:'' Keyhive ciphertext under opaque addresses; its content key and identity remain D. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:65:| `face-atom` `face-atom-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's random atom seed, one per (vessel, PersonaGroup), the device edge's delegate and countersigner and the face's Keyhive Individual. The row's file name carries the SHA-256 digest of its PersonaGroup, so no clear file names a face, and the face-atom custody contract of `@lararium/mesh` (`face-atom-custody.ts`) holds stand, read and keep: absent mints, the same bytes read as a no-op, other bytes refuse as `FaceAtomConflict`. It rests under the vessel key until the K15.6 fence moves it under that face's FCK; it never rides a bundle, a wire or a board. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:66:| `face-atom-ask` `face-atom-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the seed a founding rests before its PersonaGroup exists, named by the digest of the founding's own ask (hearth true name, binding mode, mount flag and compartment); the group row keeps the seed once the group stands and the ask row retires with the bootstrap entry. Same key class and fence as `face-atom`; it never rides a bundle. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:67:| `face-owner` `custody-holder.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's own label, sealed under its custody key: its custody id and the digest of its PersonaGroup. After a face unlocks, the holder compares this row with the floor index entry and refuses by name on a mismatch before it seats anything. Never rides a bundle. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:72:| `persona-roster` `node-vessel-identity.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' each face keeps its own root line at `faces/<fcid>/.persona-roster-h<N>.json`, selected by handle index (= ordinal). No shared roster stands: the floor index names the faces, and a locked `persona list` prints those public indices alone. `bundle: lines` carries the one line that names the face's root. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:77:| `face-address-secret` `fleet-join-custody.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's fleet address secret rests in that face, `face-address-secret-g<sha256 of its PersonaGroup>.bin`; the name's digest is the group digest the floor index holds. Local unless a defined face recovery route includes it. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:83:| `hosting-state` `hosting-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the hosting face is the face whose hosting leaf authorizes the service. Its state rests in that face, `hosting-h<N>/<aid digest>/state.json`; the Nexus AID proves no face, so the binding is the face's own directory for that AID (never the floor index), found by directory name across the face directories. The first roll founds it under the face the vessel wears and refuses by name (`HostingFaceAbsent`) where it wears none. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:86:| `walk` `node-walk-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the walking face owns its private walk record, `walk-h<N>-<gate digest>.json` in that face; a vessel still walks at one hearth (every face's names are read), and the daemon lists only the unlocked faces' walks. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:88:| `transition-pending` `seal-ceremony.ts` | floor-plain | ''F:'' field audit: a crossing in progress holds public key-sets, signatures and witnesses and no secret, so it rests in the clear in the seal home (`plain-rows.ts`), readable with no key, written under the custody claim. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:89:| `transitions` `seal-ceremony.ts` | floor-plain | ''F:'' field audit: each sealed crossing record is a verified public record (key-sets, signatures, witnesses), so it rests in the clear beside the charter and verifies from the charter alone. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:106:<<~ ahu #/row-census-browser>>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:108:!!! Row census — browser
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:114:| `vessel-key` | ''F/D split:'' public vessel contact/routing material F; any face identity seed D by its PersonaGroup. Retire the browser common private device seed and S key. ''LEAD:'' audit consumers of current seed before deletion. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:141:''Node S register.'' The present private place signing seed is a named candidate S, with the two unresolved treatments below (`vault-carriers.ts:240-242`; `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`). The existing SK tree has *zero* serving payload rows (`vault-carriers.ts:12-14,249-251`), so SK is not a justification for a common unlock. Future ember serving rows enter S only with their own row names, principal, opener and restart rule. No browser, phone, installed web app, tablet, CLI, MCP, watcher or probe owns S (`stable-founding-road.mem:207`). A container inherits the node's actual S set and cannot create one by packaging.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:170:# ''Isolation red, every row:'' found A and B with independently random FCKs/trees, occupied D carriers for both, and F plus any named node S values. Unlock A alone. Bypass routers, sessions, UI and store adapters; try direct authenticated open, occupied-row replacement, delete, rotation, backup and restore on *each* B carrier using every A key (FCK, member, identity, content, outbox, recovery), all floor values, and all node S/S key legacy values. Every B operation refuses cryptographically and leaves each B occupied ciphertext byte-for-byte unchanged. Copy A ciphertext into B's slot and swap row name/kind: authentication fails. A's same-row replacement succeeds. Restore A's bundle on a fresh vessel: B identity, key, archive and identifiers are absent; B stays unopened. Remove A: B and F still work. This red is stronger than owner-route refusal (`stable-founding-road.mem:459`; `sealed-writer.ts:279-304`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:174:# ''Tablet waking floor:'' unattended public/ciphertext sync succeeds; direct D decrypt or transformation fails until that face's session is admitted. The open product requirement for unattended *private* sync cannot silently borrow FCK (`stable-founding-road.mem:207`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:176:# ''Probe / Mudlet seat:'' with A admitted, request B through the node and by direct local ciphertext open. Both refuse; the probe retains no FCK or node S. ''LEAD:'' probe adapter implementation is outside this carrier census.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:177:# ''Node daemon / hearth:'' boot with no face admission and no omnibus key; F serves. Admit A and run the isolation red over every B node carrier, including archive, roster, pending join and outbox. Lock/restart drops volatile face keys. Hearth composition grants no extra row principal. Separately verify the place signer only under whichever OPEN JOINT option is ruled (`vault-carriers.ts:239-398`; `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-487`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:178:# ''Herm / crossroads:'' zero face rows and zero current serving rows; public card/relay service works before any face. No private seed leaks to output. Reboot drops raised ephemeral caps. The place signer's boot behavior follows the OPEN JOINT ruling, not an assumed F classification (`vault-carriers.ts:12-14,240-256`; `stable-founding-road.mem:207`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:183:# ''Generic worker host / LarVessel:'' giving a worker A's context and bypassing its router still fails to open or replace B; worker lifetime changes availability only. Public floor and ciphertext carriage continue without face keys.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:192:''K15.0, this gate:'' freeze the exhaustive node/browser row census, prove each split and owner selector, define FCK/tree/recovery and carrier context, specify old-shape refusal and the isolation red. No identity or custody bytes move. ''K15.1:'' use the existing two-hive same-process isolation probe, then give each face its own store, registry, archive and key seat. ''K15.2:'' make the face the sole identity/group owner; capture two-face event bytes and reject any shared creator/issuer. ''K15.3:'' route sessions and registries by exactly one face and land ''F6 slice three'' asker sealing with the correct row-class key and occupied-row proof. ''K15.4:'' separate content-key rolls and removal by face, including K12 fresh group behavior. ''K15.5:'' one-face restore and a herm that carries without face authoring. ''K15.6:'' one migration fence for identity bytes, split stores, FCK slot trees, archives and custody formats; refuse old mixed archives by name. This follows `stable-founding-road.mem:459,507`. ''B1'' consumes browser no-S key, per-tab face asks, slot-before-first-secret and last-tab floor (`:199-202,206-207`). F6 routing does not precede the key boundary.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:196:<<~ ahu #/the-floor-index>>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:198:!!! The floor index of faces (ruled 2026-10-23)
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:202:''The accepted leak, and only it:'' the count of the node's faces, tombstones included (so a removal history leaks as a count); each PersonaGroup's digest; each founding ask's digest; and each tree's random filename. Nothing else: no name, no handle, no prefix, no label, no key byte, and nothing derived from the face custody id beyond the filename itself. The digests already name the carriers on disk (`face-atom-g<digest>.bin`, `veil-archive-g<digest>.bin`), so the index shows a stolen disk no fact it does not already show. A removed face leaves a tombstone entry, so no other face's local ordinal moves.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:206:''The owner in every D context is the face custody id (`fcid`),'' a random 16-byte id minted with the face's slot tree at the founding's start. It is immutable and never reused. Rows that exist before the PersonaGroup does (the persona root, the founding's atom ask) seal under it, and so do the rows after, so nothing re-seals when the group arrives. The anchors row binds the fcid to the PersonaGroup. Rows are local and never cross vessels, so the id needs no cross-vessel stability.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:219:: ''One child derives today.'' The only call that reaches `holder.derive` is `custodyGateDoor` (`custody-seat.ts`), and its only consumers are `hearthSovereignPin`, `stoodSovereignPin` and the gate composition in `open-node-vessel.ts`: each derives the SOVEREIGN GATE BUNDLE (`GATE_BUNDLE_INFO`) of one Nexus and route. The registry (`ALL_DOMAINS`) declares other domains, and the door derives under any of them, but no other caller derives. The veil, Keyhive signer and hosting key named in the root's header derive from the vessel key, a face's atom or their own rows, never from this root.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:224:: ''Owner: the place, not a face.'' The archive is minted at the place card (`ensurePlaceCard`, `init`) from the vessel's own seed before any face stands; a faceless or joinee place holds one. It carries the place Individual's membership and prekey secrets and its contact card. It is a NODE-ONLY secret and enters S as the separately named row `place-archive`. Each face's own archive already rests per PersonaGroup as `veil-archive-g<digest>` (D, ''face-hot'').
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:225:: ''No identity above the faces.'' The place Individual signs no face's act and holds no face's key; the daemon island restores each face's own veil from that face's FCK row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:231:!!! The place seed's reach (ruled 2026-10-19)
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:233:* ''The veil leaves the seed.'' `deriveDyadVeil(vesselSeed, groupTag)` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/dyad.ts`) and `groupSecretOpenerFromSeed` (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`) make the vessel seed an ancestor of every face's device veil and group secret. Each becomes D: the veil mints at random at the join and rests under that face's FCK; the opener reads the face's own key. The isolation red gains the row: a thief holding the place seed derives no veil and opens no group secret of any face.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:234:* ''The veil stays with its atom.'' A face's veil rests under that face's FCK on that vessel and rides no one-face bundle; a restore onto a fresh vessel mints a fresh atom and never resurrects the dead one (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation">> #/identity-as-bond, Law 3). The one-face bundle's never-carries list gains the veil.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:235:* ''The census sorts by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Each present use of a vessel seed, on node and browser alike, sorts by the capability it serves: a floor duty goes to the place signer, which a vessel holds only while it stands a floor; an act on a face's behalf (a dial, a join, an enrolment, a sibling channel, a daemon proof) goes to that face's atom; nothing else keeps a device-wide key. The browser's device seed (`open-browser-vessel.ts`: the Keyhive Individual, the oracle proof, daemon auth, sibling enrolment, the group-secret opener) and the node's (`open-node-vessel.ts`) take the same sort.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:236:* ''The seed's other reach narrows to an allowlist.'' The online place signer serves the floor duties the roadmap's place-signer ruling enumerates; every other present use (the daemon's auth, the device-key signer, the internal asks) either names its domain on that allowlist or takes a key of its own.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:252:''The sovereign gate.'' The daemon composes sovereign when S stands held AND the worn face stands unlocked (a place with no face needs S alone); otherwise the floor composes. `sovereignStands()` reads this as a pure query. `lares vault lock --face N` drops one face; locking the worn face, or locking S, stands the vessel back at the floor through the same gate, and a sibling's lock leaves sovereign standing. The founding sweep of seeds runs under the gate only.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:256:''Status prints a face as one line:'' its handle index, a custody-id prefix, the count of rows under its key, and the group and ask digests the floor index names. A face's row never prints by name; only a fault does.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:263:# ''Node private place signing seed'' (ruled 2026-10-19: a scoped online signer under a pre-rotated place KEL whose next key rides the founding card, built in the founding bake; the options it settled follow). Current `.vessel-key*.json` contains a private signing seed in a floor file and `loadVesselSigningSeed` reads it without a human route (`vault-carriers.ts:240-242`; `node-vessel-identity.ts:429-442`). ''Option A:'' keep a *named floor signer* owned by the node, protected at rest under an explicit mechanism; floor means no custody S key/FCK, while this narrowly scoped signer can support faceless Herm startup. Specify the protection, allowed signing/derivation domains, and restart behavior. ''Option B:'' put that signer behind an explicit boot custody door; public card/relay can stand before unlock, while operations requiring its signature wait/refuse until the door opens. Specify Herm boot and unattended container behavior. Neither option is selected here. The private seed is never F, never the current S key, and never the empty serving SK.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:266:# ''Guest-owned store.'' Prove whether the guest persists its own keys/rows. If yes, it is a separate vessel with its own D/F split, FCK trees, floor, and isolation red; if no, every private guest act remains under the host's admitted face session. Host keys never silently become guest keys (`stable-founding-road.mem:207`).
